index 67c9ab7..23cca65 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -128,6 +128,32 @@ convert your own `.pt` (needs torch, `pip install '.[convert]'`):
 python convert_ifv2_to_jax.py --schema intellifold/af3_schema.pkl --v2-pt intellifold_v2.pt --out-dir model_v2
 ```
 
+#### IntelliFold-v2-flash on the JAX engine
+
+The upstream hosted JAX checkpoint is the 3.2 GB full-v2 model. This fork also
+supports the smaller v2-flash architecture, including its learned advanced
+diffusion-conditioning path. Convert the local PyTorch checkpoint once:
+
+```bash
+PYTHONPATH=. python -m intellifold.convert_flash \
+  --schema intellifold/af3_schema.pkl \
+  --flash-pt ~/.intellifold/intellifold_v2_flash.pt \
+  --out-dir model_v2_flash
+```
+
+Then select it explicitly at inference time:
+
+```bash
+intellifold predict fold_input.json --v2-flash \
+  --model-dir model_v2_flash --output-dir results -- \
+  --norun_data_pipeline
+```
+
+On Apple Silicon also pass `--flash xla` before `--` and
+`--jax_backend=mps` after it. A directory input loads the checkpoint once and
+processes its JSON files sequentially, amortising model loading and JAX
+compilation; it is directory batching, not a tensor batch.
+
 
